---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Kokoro speech"
  description="Use local Kokoro WASM narration in SuiteCut."
  section="kokoro"
>
  <p class="kicker">Field manual · 03</p>
  <h1>Kokoro speech</h1>
  <p>
    Kokoro 82M runs in a Node worker through <code>onnxruntime-web</code>. Inference stays local; no
    hosted model API or speech key is required.
  </p>

  <h2>Choose a voice</h2>
  <CodeBlock
    code={`await suitecut.narrate('The final report is ready.', {
  voice: 'af_heart',
  speed: 1,
  caption: 'The final report is ready.',
})`}
  />
  <p>
    SuiteCut supports the 28 English Kokoro voices used by Spek. Useful starting points include
    <code>af_heart</code>, <code>af_bella</code>, <code>am_michael</code>, <code>bf_emma</code>, and
    <code>bm_george</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Bundled default</h2>
  <p>
    The npm package includes the quantized model, tokenizer, and <code>af_heart</code> voice. The default
    voice works without a download or network request.
  </p>
  <div class="note">
    Other supported voices download on first use and remain in the local cache. Set
    <code>SUITECUT_MODEL_CACHE</code> to choose another cache directory.
  </div>

  <h2>Timeline behavior</h2>
  <p>
    Narrations are serialized. SuiteCut pauses frame ingestion during synthesis, then records each
    caption for the measured audio duration. Model startup time does not appear in the video.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
